Fillets: the walk of WalkedOnSameToEndFace past the end of the face N it
takes unbounded runs on past the end of the curve N is an extrusion of
(mitcad#1345).

WalkedOnSameToEndFace (patch 0600) walks an OnSame end's
last piece again with the surface of the face N its contact left
unbounded, past the spine's end vertex, up to where the other contact
reaches the edge between its face and the face at the end. A face made by
extruding a profile's spline stretch is a surface of linear extrusion of a
B-spline curve covering that stretch alone, bounded by the stretch's ends.
A fin's end face is one: its two side edges rounded with 1 up to the top,
each side's walk past its chain's top vertex runs its contact on the end
face over the top, past the stretch's end at the top's crease. The walk
fell off the surface there at once, no corner was made, and the two
sides' roundings were taken for intersecting. A stored state whose end
face is the extrusion of the whole spline builds the same rounding.

Where N's surface is such an extrusion, its curve is now run on past the
end nearer P's contact on N by four radii, curvature continuously
(GeomLib::ExtendCurveToPoint, third order, up to the curve's own
polynomial run on there), its parameters kept. On the reported fin the
run on lies on the whole spline's extrusion within 1e-4 mm over the first
1.6 mm and 5.5e-4 mm over four.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_fin_end.cpp, the reported fin's end
rounded along its sides on the body MitCad builds: the rounding builds,
closed, and the stored body after it lies on the result within 0.01 mm
round the end (the rounding fails without the patch).

Upstream: new.

